<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ozolua</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1480–<a href="/years/1504">1504</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Oba Ozolua, Ozolua the Conqueror</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ozolua, known as Ozolua the Conqueror, was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> who reigned c. 1480–1504. Under him the Benin Empire achieved its greatest military successes. He also established diplomatic and commercial relations with the Portuguese from 1485, bringing brass <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manilla">manillas</a> into Benin that supplied the casting of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-bronzes">Benin Bronzes</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ozolua.jpg" alt="Ozolua" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GuillaumeG · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oba_Ozolua_-_MCN_4185_(cropped2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
